//RS /// c125 P0 regression guard: a runtime stop under the default JIT backend
//RS /// (list index OOB here; the same trapped-flag mechanism covers checked-arith
//RS /// overflow and the two concurrency panic sites) must report cleanly — not
//RS /// kill the resident process. The next hot-reload iteration in the SAME
//RS /// process must then run cleanly, proving the trap didn't leak into the next
//RS /// run's heap and the process is still alive to serve it. Before the fix,
//RS /// every one of these host shims called `std::process::exit(70)` directly,
//RS /// which took the whole `jet dev` server down with it.
//RS ///
//RS /// The reported shape is `Ran { exit_code: 70 }` carrying the registered
//RS /// `Stop [E3010]`, NOT `Problems`. #1483 (0a291f5bb) retired the old
//RS /// `Problems(E0953)` route precisely because a live-program trap is not a
//RS /// comptime build failure; `jit_1216_adversarial_regressions` and
//RS /// `uninit_fixed_dynamic_oob_uses_the_resident_jit_trap_path` pin the same
//RS /// contract for the same OOB shape, and AOT `jet_panic` agrees (I9).
//RS #[test]
//RS fn cranelift_trap_then_hot_swap_continues() {
//RS     // Session-scoped boundary; see `cranelift_hot_swap_preserves_live_state`.
//RS     with_jit_test_scope(cranelift_trap_then_hot_swap_continues_inner);
//RS }
