//RS /// #2020: every `tests/dev_parts/*.rs` slice is wired into a real cargo test
//RS /// target.
//RS ///
//RS /// The suite was split because one binary could not run its own declared tests
//RS /// inside the 900s guard, and a split has exactly one silent failure mode: a
//RS /// slice that no `tests/dev*.rs` target `include!`s compiles nowhere and runs
//RS /// nowhere, so its tests stop existing without anything going red. That is the
//RS /// shape that let five `jit_run` failures sit unrecorded for a whole session —
//RS /// the tests were not in a routine set and nothing said so.
//RS ///
//RS /// Naming the target is all it takes to be routine: cargo makes a test binary
//RS /// out of every `tests/*.rs` file by itself, and `Tools/ci/test-shards.sh`
//RS /// enumerates the whole target inventory fresh on every run (D-CI1=A). So the
//RS /// only thing left to check is that no slice is orphaned.
